<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 23_semantics_accessibility/13: Buttons versus links -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Buttons versus links</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .panel { background: #fff; border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .panel a, .panel button { display: inline-block; margin: 0.3rem; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; font: inherit; }
    .panel a { background: #e0f2fe; color: #075985; }
    .panel button { border: 0; background: #0f172a; color: #fff; cursor: pointer; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Buttons versus links</h1>
    <p class="lead">Links go somewhere; buttons do something.</p>
    <section class="panel">
      <a href="#settings">Open settings</a> navigates to a page.
      <br><button type="button">Save changes</button> runs an action.
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
